  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "Failures stem from memory ranking by raw overlap alone: the top-ranked memory item is a stale/high-overlap record (age 18-20) that crowds out the correct current record (age 0, entity_match=1) which sits just below the top_k=2 cutoff, and in scope cases a non-entity-matching item outranks the entity-matching one. A general scoring function that rewards entity_match, scope_match, trusted, available, read_only and recency (penalizing age) while still using overlap as a tiebreaker will surface the correct current record within top_k, letting the model answer instead of defaulting to UNKNOWN. Separately, tool_routing picks an unavailable preview tool over the available current registry, and tool_recovery never retries transient errors; but only memory_score and memory_top_k are changeable here, so the fix targets memory ranking.",
