    "predicted_behavior": "The correct current record (age 0, entity_match=1, scope_match=1) gains a recency bonus and entity/scope bonuses that lift it above stale high-overlap records and non-entity-matching distractors, so it enters the top_k=3 memory set. The model then has the needed channel/tier facts and returns the requested value with correct evidence IDs instead of UNKNOWN, improving memory_temporal, memory_scope, and composition families while leaving tool routing/recovery behavior unchanged.",
    "regression_risk": "Raising top_k to 3 adds one extra memory item per query, slightly increasing prompt noise and token cost; the recency term could over-favor a fresh but low-overlap irrelevant record in rare cases, and the fixed weights are heuristic rather than learned, so some queries where overlap was the only reliable signal may rank slightly differently. Tool_routing and tool_recovery failures are not addressed by this change and will persist."
